ling of Sundance 6 On Nov. 2, 2026, the Company provided notice to the Alberta Electric System Operator (AESO) that Battle River Units 4 and 5 will be mothballed effective March 1, 2027, for a period of time up to Jan. 1, 2029 and extended the mothballing of Sundance 6 for a period of time up to April 1, 2029. The Company maintains the flexibility to return the mothballed units to service when market fundamentals improve or contracting opportunities are secured. Battle River Units 4 and 5 will remain available and fully operational through to March 1, 2027. Sale of minority interest in Oklahoma wind portfolio On Oct. 22, 2026, the Company completed the sale of a 49 per cent minority ownership interest in its 500 MW Oklahoma wind portfolio to Ares Infrastructure funds for cash proceeds of US$305 million, before customary closing adjustments. The portfolio comprises the 100 MW White Rock West, 200 MW White Rock East and 200 MW Horizon Hill wind facilities. The Company will continue to provide operational oversight under a long-term\n"}
{"page": 9, "text": "asset management agreement. Acquisition of Mountain Peak Power and Canyon Peak Power and associated public offering of common shares On Oct. 22, 2026, the Company closed the acquisition of Mountain Peak Power and Canyon Peak Power, two fully contracted natural gas-fired peaking facilities totaling 318 MW near Denver, Colorado from an indirect subsidiary of Blackstone, Inc. (the Acquisition). The purchase price for the Acquisition was US$1 billion, including the assumption of US$750 million of project debt. On June 9, 2026 the Company closed a public offering of 18,230,000 common shares at a price of $19.20 per share through a syndicate of underwriters, for total gross proceeds of approximately $350 million, which was used to fund the cash portion of the purchase price for the Acquisition. The proceeds received in advance of the Acquisition were partially used to repay the drawn amounts under the syndicated credit facility.\nM6 TransAlta Corporation\nCentralia Unit 2 Mandated to Remain Available for additional 90 days On Sept. 14, 2026, the Company received another order from the U.S. Department of Energy (the Order) requiring that our 700 MW Centralia Unit 2 facility (Facility) remain available for operation for an additional period of 90 days, until Dec. 12, 2026. As previously communicated, the Company has been subject to the Order from the U.S. Department of Energy since Dec. 16, 2025. The Company continues to comply with the Order and continues to work with the federal and state governments in relation thereto. The Facility had no generation during the nine months ended Sept. 30, 2026. Declaration of Common Share Dividend On Oct. 27, 2026, TransAlta's Board of Directors approved a quarterly dividend payment of $0.070 per common share payable on Jan. 1, 2027. Operating and Financial Performance Operating Performance Availability The following table provides availability (%) by segment:\n3 months ended Sept. 30, 9 months ended Sept. 30,\n2026 