{"page": 11, "text": "In addition to availability, the Company uses long\u2011term average (LTA) generation as a key performance indicator for its renewable facilities, comparing actual production to expected long\u2011term output. While Hydro and Wind and Solar production can vary period to period, over longer durations, facilities are expected to perform in-line with their LTA, which represents an annualized energy output expected from our facilities based on historical resource data, observed operating performance and forward\u2011looking assumptions about future conditions. LTA generation is not applicable to the Gas segment, as these dispatchable facilities operate based on market conditions, and merchant and customer demand. Total production for the three and nine months ended Sept. 30, 2026, decreased by 891 and 2,372 GWh, or 14 and 13 per cent, respectively, compared to the same periods in 2025, primarily due to: \u2022No production at Centralia Unit 2 in the Energy Transition segment. Refer to the \"Description of the Business\" section of this MD&A; and \u2022Higher dispatch optimization in Alberta in the Gas segment due to lower market prices; and \u2022Retirement of the Ada Cogeneration facility in the U.S. in Jan. 2026; partially offset by \u2022Higher production volumes in the Wind and Solar segment due to higher wind resource; and \u2022Higher production in the Gas segment due to the addition of the Far North facilities. Total production for the nine months ended Sept. 30, 2026 was further impacted by higher production in the Hydro segment due to higher water resource. Financial Performance Review of Consolidated Information\n3 months ended Sept. 30, 9 months ended Sept. 30,\n2026 2025 2026 2025\nRevenues 536 615 1,588 1,806\nGross Margin 411 353 1,205 1,119\nOperations, maintenance and administration (174) (179) (530) (525)\nDepreciation and amortization (104) (135) (314) (431)\nInterest expense (75) (85) (241) (266)\nEarnings (loss) before income taxes 100 (53) 203 (99)\nNet earnings (loss) attributable to common shareholders 63 (62) 111 (128)\nAdjusted Earnings before Income Taxes(1) 91 17 226 167\nAdjusted Net Earnings (Loss) Attributable to Common Shareholders(1) 56 (8) 128 76\n(1)These are non-IFRS measures. Refer to the \"Non-IFRS and Supplementary Financial Measures\" section of this MD&A. Three months ended Sept. 30, 2026 Variance Analysis (2026 versus 2025) Revenues for the three months ended Sept. 30, 2026, decreased by $79 million, or 13 per cent, compared to the same period in 2025, primarily due to: \u2022No production at Centralia Unit 2; \u2022Lower revenue from the Sarnia gas facility due to contract renewal at a lower price and the retirement of the Ada Cogeneration facility; and \u2022Lower revenues in the Gas and Hydro segments due to lower spot and ancillary services prices in the Alberta market, partially offset by higher merchant and ancillary\nM8 TransAlta Corporation\n"}
{"page": 12, "text": "services volumes in the Hydro segment; partially offset by \u2022Higher unrealized mark-to-market gains on derivatives primarily due to a decrease in forward market prices and forecasted volumes in the current period; \u2022Higher revenues in the Gas segment from the addition of the Far North facilities; and \u2022Higher revenues in the Wind and Solar segment due to higher wind resource across all regions. Mark-to-market gains in the current period were also impacted by the adoption of IFRS 9 hedge accounting, effective Jan. 1, 2026. Refer to the \"Material Accounting Policies, Accounting Changes and Critical Accounting Estimates\" section of this MD&A for details. Gross Margin for the three months ended Sept. 30, 2026, increased by $58 million, or 16 per cent, compared to the same period in 2025, primarily due to: \u2022Higher carbon compliance recovery due to the planned utilization of emission credits, which reduced the 2026 carbon compliance obligation in the current period; partially offset by \u2022The factors which decreased revenues as explained above. OM&A expenses for the three months ended Sept. 30, 2026 decreased by $5 million, or three per cent, compared to the same period in 2025, primarily due to: \u2022Lower spending due to one-time costs incurred during the prior period and current period saving initiatives; and \u2022Lower spending following the successful completion of an upgrade to our enterprise resource planning (ERP) system; partially offset by \u2022Higher spending associated with Centralia Unit 2 to comply with the Order; and \u2022Addition of OM&A from the acquisition of the Far North facilities. Depreciation and amortization for the three months ended Sept. 30, 2026, decreased by $31 million, or 23 per cent, compared to the same period in 2025, primarily due to: \u2022Lower depreciation in the Gas segment in the current period due to a change in the useful life assumptions in 2025 for the Sheerness facilities; and \u2022Lower depreciation for Centralia Unit 2 due to the cessation of coal-fired operations in the normal course. Interest expense for the three months ended Sept. 30, 2026, decreased by $10 million, or 12 per cent, compared to 2025, primarily due to lower interest on certain senior notes following their refinancing at lower interest rates during 2025 and lower average outstanding debt. Earnings before income taxes for the three months ended Sept. 30, 2026, increased by $153 million, or 289 per cent, from loss before income taxes in the same period in 2025, primarily due to the items noted above. Net earnings attributable to common shareholders for the three months ended Sept. 30, 2026, increased by $125 million, or 202 per cent, from net loss attributable to common shareholders in the same period of 2025, primarily due to: \u2022The items noted above; partially offset by \u2022Higher income taxes due to an increase in earnings before income taxes. Adjusted Earnings before Income Taxes for the three months ended Sept. 30, 2026, increased by $74 million, or 435 per cent,\n"}
{"page": 13, "text": "compared to the same period in 2025, primarily due to: \u2022The factors causing higher Adjusted EBITDA described in the \"Adjusted EBITDA\" section of this MD&A; and \u2022Lower depreciation and amortization, and lower interest expense as explained above. Adjusted Net Earnings Attributable to Common Shareholders for the three months ended Sept. 30, 2026 increased from Adjusted Net Loss attributable to Common Shareholders in the same period in 2025 primarily due to higher Adjusted Earnings before Income Taxes as explained above. Nine months ended Sept. 30, 2026 Variance Analysis (2026 versus 2025) Revenues for the nine months ended Sept. 30, 2026 totalled $1,588 million, a decrease of $218 million, or 12 per cent, compared to the same period in 2025, primarily due to: \u2022No production at Centralia Unit 2; \u2022Lower revenues for the Hydro and Gas segments due to lower spot and ancillary services prices in the Alberta market, net of favourable hedge pricing; \u2022Lower revenue from the Sarnia gas facility due to a contract renewal at a lower price and the retirement of the Ada Cogeneration facility; and \u2022Lower environmental and tax attributes revenues in the Hydro segment due to lower sales of emission credits to third parties; partially offset by \u2022Higher unrealized mark-to-market gains on derivatives primarily due to a decrease in forward market prices and forecasted volumes, and an increase in favourable hedge positions settled, which generated positive contributions over settled spot prices; \u2022Higher merchant revenues in the Gas segment in Eastern Canada driven by higher realized prices and generation; and\nTransAlta Corporation M9\n"}
