r cent, from loss before income taxes in the same period in 2025, primarily due to: \u2022The items noted above; \u2022Higher asset impairment reversals primarily related to a change in the discount rates on decommissioning and restoration provisions on retired assets; \u2022An impairment charge, net of impairment reversals, in the comparative period related to certain Wind and Solar facilities due to changes in expected production volumes and price assumptions; \u2022Higher unrealized and realized foreign exchange gains mainly due to favourable changes in foreign currency rates; and \u2022Higher other operating income due to legal settlement recoveries; partially offset by \u2022Impairment reversal in the comparative period related to generation equipment classified as held for sale. Net earnings attributable to common shareholders for the nine months ended Sept. 30, 2026 increased by $239 million, or 187 per cent, from net loss attributable to common shareholders in the same period in 2025, primarily due to: \u2022The items noted above; partially offset by \u2022Higher income taxes due to\n"}
{"page": 15, "text": "an increase in earnings before income taxes, and \u2022Higher net earnings attributable to non-controlling interests in the current period. Adjusted Earnings before Income Taxes for the nine months ended Sept. 30, 2026, increased by $59 million, or 35 per cent, compared to the same period in 2025, primarily due to: \u2022The factors causing lower Adjusted EBITDA described in the \"Adjusted EBITDA\" section of this MD&A; partially offset by \u2022Lower depreciation and amortization, and lower interest expense as explained above. Adjusted Net Earnings Attributable to Common Shareholders for the nine months ended Sept. 30, 2026, increased by $52 million, or 68 per cent, compared to the same period in 2025, primarily due to: \u2022The factors causing higher Adjusted Earnings before Income Taxes explained above and the associated tax effect; partially offset by \u2022Higher net earnings attributable to non-controlling interests as explained above. Refer to the \"Segmented Financial Performance and Operating Results by Geographical Location\" section for additional information.\nM10 TransAlta Corporation\nAdjusted EBITDA1 For the three months ended Sept. 30, 2026, the Company's Adjusted EBITDA increased by $26 million, or 11 per cent, compared to the same period in 2025. For the nine months ended Sept. 30, 2026, the Company's Adjusted EBITDA decreased by $98 million, or 11 per cent, compared to the same period in 2025. The segments impacting Adjusted EBITDA are summarized as follows:\nQ3 2026 vs Q3 2025 YTD 2026 vs YTD 2025\n(1)Adjusted EBITDA is a non-IFRS measure. Refer to the \"Non-IFRS and Supplementary Financial Measures\" section of this MD&A. For the three and nine months ended Sept. 30, 2026, the most directly comparable IFRS measure is earnings before income taxes of $100 million and $203 million, respectively (loss before income taxes of $53 million and $99 million for the three and nine months ended Sept. 30, 2025). Refer to the \"Reconciliation of Non-IFRS Measures on a Consolidated Basis by Segments\" section of this MD&A. Free Cash Flow1 For the three and nine months ended Sept. 30, 2026, the Company's FCF decreased by $12 million, or 11 per cent, and $83 million, or 20 per cent, respectively, compared to the same periods in 2025. The major factors impacting FCF are summarized as follows:\nQ3 2026 vs Q3 2025 YTD 2026 vs YTD 2025\n"}
